%N A387532 Numbers k in A005117 such that k+1 is in A001694.
%C A387532 A subsequence of A359749. Related to the search for further terms of A388967.
%C A387532 From _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 20 2026: (Start)
%C A387532 Squarefree numbers that are followed by a powerful number.
%C A387532 The numbers of terms that do not exceed the (10^m)-th powerful number A376092(m), for m = 1, 2, ..., are 6, 56, 572, 5835, 58735, 589339, 5903069, 59073787, ... .
%C A387532 It appears that the relative asymptotic density of the powerful numbers k+1 within the sequence of powerful numbers exists and equals 0.59... .
%C A387532 {A067874(n)^2-1, n >= 1} is a subsequence that corresponds to the squarefree numbers k such that k+1 is a square. (End)
%H A387532 Pontus von Brömssen, <a href="/A387532/b387532.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a> (first 1168 terms from N. J. A. Sloane)
%H A387532 <a href="/index/Pow#powerful">Index entries for sequences related to powerful numbers</a>.
%t A387532 q[k_] := SquareFreeQ[k] && AllTrue[FactorInteger[k+1][[;;, 2]], # > 1 &]; Select[Range[3500], q] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 20 2026 *)
%o A387532 (PARI) isok(k) = issquarefree(k) && ispowerful(k+1); \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 20 2026
